[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ar:Louis G.Alexander]
[ti:141. Sally's First Train Ride]
[by:Generated by iChochy]

[00:00.467] Lesson 141. | 第141课。
[00:05.047] Last week, my four-year-old daughter /ˈdɔːtə/ Sally was invited to a children's party. | 上周，我四岁的女儿萨莉被邀请去参加一个儿童派对。
[00:12.477] I decided /dɪˈsaɪdɪd/ to take her by train. | 我决定带她乘火车去。
[00:16.117] Sally was very excited /ɪkˈsaɪtɪd/ because she had never traveled on a train before. | 萨莉非常兴奋，因为她以前从未坐过火车。
[00:22.427] She sat near the window and asked questions about everything she saw. | 她坐在窗边，问她所看到的一切问题。
[00:28.987] Suddenly, a middle-aged /ˌmɪdl ˈeɪdʒd/ lady came into our compartment /kəmˈpɑːtmənt/ and sat opposite /ˈɒpəzɪt/ Sally. | 突然，一位中年女士走进我们的车厢，坐在萨莉的对面。
[00:36.317] "Hello, little girl," she said. | “你好，小姑娘，”她说。
[00:40.247] Sally did not answer, but looked at her curiously /ˈkjʊəriəsli/. | 萨莉没有回答，只是好奇地看着她。
[00:45.107] The lady was dressed in a blue coat and a large funny /ˈfʌni/ hat. | 那位女士穿着一件蓝色外套和一顶又大又滑稽的帽子。
[00:51.317] After the train had left the station, the lady opened her handbag and took out her powder /ˈpaʊdə/ compact /ˈkɒmpækt/. | 火车离开车站后，那位女士打开手提包，拿出她的粉饼盒。
[00:59.847] She then began /bɪˈɡæn/ to make up /ˌmeɪk ˈʌp/ her face. | 然后她开始化妆。
[01:03.527] "Why are you doing that?" Sally asked. | “你为什么要这样做？”萨莉问。
[01:08.147] "To make myself beautiful," the lady answered. | “为了让自己变漂亮，”那位女士回答。
[01:13.217] She put away her compact /ˈkɒmpækt/ and smiled kindly /ˈkaɪndli/. | 她收好粉饼盒，友好地笑了笑。
[01:18.417] "But you are still ugly /ˈʌɡli/," Sally said. | “但你仍然很丑，”萨莉说。
[01:22.907] Sally was amused /əˈmjuːzd/, but I was very embarrassed /ɪmˈbærəst/. | 萨莉觉得好笑，但我却非常尴尬。
